pr.body:
Refs ed3c/soodles#51

This candidate adds only the N-class report for the behavior-first P-class deletion eval. `AGENTS.md` is byte-identical to `main`; the proposed deletion was not retained.

Observed result:

- first 18-run trial preserved as invalid after the frozen observer crashed on an unspecified receipt representation;
- replacement observer corrected and frozen under a separate supervisor boundary;
- 18 fresh replacement cloud consumers completed;
- arm-blind audit was committed before unblinding;
- frozen correctness passed 4/18 overall;
- baseline passed 3/9 and treatment 1/9 after unblinding;
- repeated explicit instruction reads were zero in every run;
- context/output bytes were telemetry only;
- baseline recovery also failed 0/3, so no causal behavior-regression claim is made.

Raw evidence and split archive manifest are pinned at commit [4802d2c](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/commit/4802d2c786ef008a7dd189078626cee099ac73a5).

The report identifies two evaluator gaps for a future atom: shell-wrapped instruction reads are not bound by the recorder, and request creation must be distinguished from provider transport. This PR does not repair those separate causes.

## Final landing receipt

Provider delivery completed, but the pinned landing checkpoint is not `RESOLVED`:

- experiment: `RETENTION_RULE_FAIL_AGENTS_UNCHANGED`; the P-class deletion was not retained and `AGENTS.md` stayed unchanged;
- PR #52 merged as `f3e54c25caac833b1ce2970aaebfb4e1d75defa0`; merge tree and ordered parents match the claim;
- Issue #51 closed with `state_reason=completed` after fresh provider readback;
- exact-head runtime evidence passed (run `35237876987`, attempt 1, job `105258368741`);
- local checkpoint advanced to `awaiting_reconcile` and then the owner refused `worktree.path=missing before cleanup intent`;
- the cloud execution never created a local `issue-51-pclass-behavior` branch/worktree, so the current owner cannot express a proved no-op cleanup; Git fetch was not reached and this must not be reported as a Git-transport failure;
- no merge or close request will be replayed.

[Delivery receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/9b7a33976a9cf35b0d1cc807d03d4659d6f0fbac/docs/experiments/pclass-behavior-51/delivery/delivery-receipt.json), [checkpoint](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/9b7a33976a9cf35b0d1cc807d03d4659d6f0fbac/docs/experiments/pclass-behavior-51/delivery/checkpoint.json), and [archive manifest](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/9b7a33976a9cf35b0d1cc807d03d4659d6f0fbac/docs/experiments/pclass-behavior-51/delivery/archive-manifest.json) preserve the handoff.

A separate smallest atom should teach the landing owner how to verify a cloud-only no-local-worktree cleanup as a no-op, then resume this exact checkpoint through the verifier migration path. Do not synthesize an unobserved worktree or edit the checkpoint by hand.

## Verifier-migration recovery observation

Issue #53 / PR #54 landed the cloud-only no-op owner fix. The existing #51 checkpoint then accepted only the new verifier digest while preserving every provider/local identity, both offered writes, and `provider_requests=[]`.

The checkpoint remains `awaiting_reconcile`. A #53 reconciliation attempt against the same control root had just persisted its no-op intent and then failed Git fetch with exit 128, so #51 did not repeat the unchanged carrier attempt. Merge and close were not replayed; #51 is not reported as `RESOLVED`.

[Recovery receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/f8f060d5d764a1be294c482362335b933d8aaa10/docs/experiments/pclass-behavior-51/delivery/recovery-receipt.json), [migrated checkpoint](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/f8f060d5d764a1be294c482362335b933d8aaa10/docs/experiments/pclass-behavior-51/delivery/recovery-checkpoint.json), and [resume result](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/f8f060d5d764a1be294c482362335b933d8aaa10/docs/experiments/pclass-behavior-51/delivery/recovery-resume-result.json) preserve the current handoff.

